<Layout title={"Mobile & WebGL | Game Nock"} description={"Mobile and WebGL game development in Unity for iOS, Android and the browser, including IAP, attribution and store submission."} active="services" contact={true}>
<section class="pg-hero"><div class="wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/services/">Services</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Mobile &amp; WebGL</span></nav><span class="eyebrow">Mobile & WebGL</span><h1>Mobile and WebGL Games Built for Real Devices.</h1><p class="lede">Unity games designed, built and tuned for iOS, Android and the browser.</p><div class="ctas"><button class="btn btn-primary mag" data-contact>Discuss Your Project <svg><use href="#arrow"/></svg></button><a class="btn btn-wa-solid" href="https://wa.me/923184142473" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg><use href="#whatsapp"/></svg> Chat on WhatsApp</a></div></div></section><section class="sp "><div class="wrap"><div class="g2"><div class="glass"><span class="eyebrow">Problems we solve</span><h2 class="ttl">When Teams Call Us</h2><ul class="facts"><li>Your game needs to run smoothly on mid-range phones</li><li>App store requirements such as ATT, deep links or IAP need to be handled</li><li>A browser version must load quickly and run well</li><li>Attribution and analytics need to be set up correctly</li></ul></div>
      <div class="glass"><span class="eyebrow">Deliverables</span><h2 class="ttl">What You Receive</h2><ul class="facts"><li>Mobile gameplay and UI</li><li>In-app purchases and advertising</li><li>Attribution, analytics and deep links</li><li>App Tracking Transparency on iOS</li><li>WebGL builds with load-time optimisation</li><li>Store preparation and submission</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="sp "><div class="wrap"><div class="g2"><div class="glass"><span class="eyebrow">Project stages</span><h2 class="ttl">Where This Fits</h2><ul class="facts"><li>New mobile or browser game</li><li>Adding a mobile or web version of an existing game</li><li>Pre-launch store preparation</li></ul></div>
      <div class="glass"><span class="eyebrow">Technologies</span><h2 class="ttl">What We Use</h2><table class="tbl"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Engine</th><td>Unity</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Platforms</th><td>iOS, Android, WebGL</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Analytics</th><td>AppsFlyer, Tenjin</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Backend</th><td>PlayFab, Firebase</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></section><section class="sp "><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head"><span class="eyebrow">Process</span><h2>How We Deliver</h2></div><ol class="ksteps"><li class="glass"><h3>Review</h3><p>We study your project and goals.</p></li><li class="glass"><h3>Plan</h3><p>Scope, team, milestones and risks.</p></li><li class="glass"><h3>Build</h3><p>Iterative development with regular builds.</p></li><li class="glass"><h3>Test</h3><p>QA on target devices.</p></li><li class="glass"><h3>Deliver</h3><p>Release, handover and support.</p></li></ol><p style="margin-top:24px"><a class="link" href="/how-we-work/">See the full process <svg><use href="#arrow"/></svg></a></p></div></section><section class="sp "><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head"><span class="eyebrow">Related work</span><h2>Projects Where We Did This</h2></div><div class="g3"><a class="glass ccard" href="/work/highnoon/" data-tags="mobile multiplayer backend"><div class="ci"><Picture src={i_02_highnoon} formats={["avif","webp"]} fallbackFormat="webp" widths={[400, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 92vw, (max-width: 1100px) 46vw, 560px" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="HighNoon key art" /></div>
  <div class="cb"><div class="tags"><span class="tag2">Mobile competitive game</span><span class="tag2">Mobile</span></div><h3 style="font-size:22px;margin:0 0 10px">HighNoon</h3><ul class="facts"><li>Real-time 1v1 multiplayer</li><li>PlayFab services</li><li>In-app purchases and advertising</li></ul><span class="more">View case study <svg><use href="#arrow"/></svg></span></div></a></div></div></section><section class="sp "><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head"><span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span><h2>Common Questions</h2></div><div class="faq"><details class="glass"><summary>Can one project ship to mobile and web?</summary><p>Often, yes. We plan quality settings and input handling early so one codebase can serve both.</p></details><details class="glass"><summary>Do you handle store submission?</summary><p>Yes. We prepare builds, metadata requirements and compliance items such as ATT, and support you through review.</p></details></div></div></section>
</Layout>
